  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strong mandatory all-incident reporting with 24-hour regulator notice and 72-hour customer notice. S2 requires 55°C testing and per-model results to customers/regulators but drops any fixed failure-rate cap, so no model is automatically barred. S3 requires new-unit shut-off in 24 months and installed-unit enablement within 6 years for capable units; S4 imposes built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 sets an 8/100k investigation trigger but makes recall contingent on a regulator material-risk determination."
